{
  "name": "Score, route and reply to inbound leads with GPT-4o-mini, Gmail, Telegram and Google Sheets",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "2015a71f-dde2-4f2d-a348-26053ae5023b",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1000,
        -320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "## Score, route and reply to inbound leads with GPT-4o-mini, Gmail, Telegram and Google Sheets\n\n### How it works\n\nAny form that can POST a webhook (Tally, Typeform, Webflow, WordPress...) sends the lead here. The form gets an instant OK, spam is dropped by a native Filter, then GPT-4o-mini rates budget, authority, need and timeline from 0 to 25 each against a JSON schema. A small Code node adds the points up, so the score is transparent and tunable. Hot leads (70+) alert you by Gmail and Telegram and get a draft reply, warm leads (40-69) get the draft only, cold leads are just logged. If the AI call fails, the lead is flagged for manual review instead of being lost. Every Monday a Telegram digest summarises the week.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Describe your business and ideal customer in the system message of the AI node.\n- Connect OpenAI, Gmail, Telegram and Google Sheets; set your chat ID, alert email and spreadsheet ID.\n- Create a \"Leads\" sheet with the columns from the Log Lead node and point your form at the webhook URL.\n\n### Customization\n\nChange thresholds in the Switch, weights and bonuses in the Code node, or swap Telegram for Slack."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c3927cd1-65e9-48ae-aecb-a6c72d0c5cb4",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -310,
        -170
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1020,
        "height": 330,
        "content": "## 1. Receive and clean the lead\n\nThe webhook accepts a POST from any form builder and answers immediately, so the form never waits for the AI. Field names are normalised and spam is dropped: invalid or disposable email, filled honeypot, empty message."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "cfb79343-0869-4a6f-ad9d-947ac03dd112",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        730,
        -170
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 800,
        "height": 570,
        "content": "## 2. Score with AI\n\nGPT-4o-mini rates budget, authority, need and timeline from 0 to 25 each. The output parser enforces the JSON schema; the Code node sums the points and adds small bonuses for a business email and a phone number."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "52657b91-ac99-4dc0-a857-302717776c8a",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1570,
        -170
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1060,
        "height": 930,
        "content": "## 3. Route and act\n\nThe Switch sends leads to Hot (70+), Warm (40-69) or Cold. Hot: Gmail and Telegram alert plus a draft reply to the lead. Warm: draft reply only. Every lead is appended to the Google Sheet."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "3fcf8581-37ff-4fa3-a880-937ac823d068",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1570,
        800
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 800,
        "height": 330,
        "content": "## Fallback: never lose a lead\n\nIf OpenAI is down or returns invalid JSON, the error output of the AI node flags the lead for manual review, logs it with tier \"Review\" and pings Telegram."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a8efac1e-c009-430f-a7bc-c533b78c44a4",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -310,
        430
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1240,
        "height": 330,
        "content": "## 4. Weekly digest\n\nEvery Monday at 9:00 the log is read, filtered to the last 7 days and summarised in one Telegram message: counts per tier, average score and the top hot leads."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "952e05aa-74ce-46d7-a2cf-7f0bdd1e10e1",
      "name": "Sticky Note6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1000,
        608
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 400,
        "content": "### 🚀 Want this wired into your stack?\n\nThis template is the safe starting point. I build extended versions for real businesses: **CRM sync** (HubSpot, Pipedrive, Zoho), **lead enrichment** (company website, LinkedIn, Clearbit), **duplicate detection**, Slack instead of Telegram, auto-reply above a confidence threshold, multi-brand and multi-language intake.\n\nAsync delivery, no calls - contact links in my creator profile."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "8120f306-b62a-47a5-ab46-e4c98434b937",
